<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's generated Info.plist because Tauri looks for this file beside
  tauri.conf.json (verified in tauri-utils, `MacConfig::info_plist`) — so there is no config entry
  to keep in sync with it.

  One key, and it exists so a permission dialog explains itself. macOS asks before an app may reach
  the local network, and the tray reaches it for one reason: a server announces the address it
  answers on, and with remote access configured that address is a hostname on the LAN rather than
  loopback. Without this string the system shows the request with no reason attached, which is the
  same "documented, not discovered" rule the README applies to Gatekeeper.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
  <string>seedeep connects to the seedeep server at the address it announces. With remote access configured that address is a name on your local network, so macOS asks first. Declining means pasting the server's URL by hand instead.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
